<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112148" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φορός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέρω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
			<i>bearing:</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b>
			<i>bringing on one's way, forwarding;</i> of a wind,
				<i>favourable,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνεμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					1.60.6
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				31.15.8
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνεῦμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					6.3.5
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				14.55
			</span></i>, etc.; so in neut. sense, <i>tending,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάτω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					908a24
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύβος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Sat.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς ὑγίειαν φ.</span>
			<i>conducive</i> to health, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				6.1.12
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φορὰ καὶ συνεργὰ πρὸς ἀρετήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.5c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>productive, fruitful,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>CP</u>
					3.20.3
				</span></i>
			; of a woman, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				1.40
			</span></i>: c. gen., <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				8.15
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φορῶς,</span> c. dat.,
			<i>conformably</i> to, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλάττουσι ἴδια φ. τῇ κατασκευῇ τῆς
					δόξης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Sign.</u>
					38
				</span></i>
			; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τὴν δόξαν</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				26
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρέπουσιν τὸ σωμάτιον φ. εἰς ἀρρωστίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ir.</u>
					p.29W.
				</span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
